## Step-by-Step Installation & Run Guide

1. **Initialize Vite React TypeScript Project**:
```bash
npm create vite@latest mubashir-portfolio -- --template react-ts
cd mubashir-portfolio

```


2. **Install Dependencies**:
```bash
npm install three framer-motion lucide-react clsx tailwind-merge
npm install -D tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer @types/three
npx tailwindcss init -p

```


3. **Replace Files**: Copy and paste the code provided above into their respective file paths (`package.json`, `index.html`, `tailwind.config.js`, `postcss.config.js`, `vite.config.ts`, `src/index.css`, `src/utils.ts`, `src/data.ts`, `src/Component.tsx`, `src/components/Navbar.tsx`, `src/components/ImageWithFallback.tsx`, `src/sections/Sections.tsx`, `src/App.tsx`, and `src/main.tsx`).
4. **Add Assets**: Create a `public/images/` directory and place your pictures with the requested filenames (or rely on the built-in gradient fallbacks):
* `/public/images/banner.webp` (1920x600)
* `/public/images/dp.webp` (800x800)
* `/public/images/headline.webp` (800x1000)
* `/public/images/about.webp` (800x1000)
* `/public/images/experience.webp` (800x1000)
* `/public/images/education.webp` (800x1000)
* `/public/images/skills.png` (800x1000)
* `/public/images/certs.webp` (800x1000)
* `/public/images/projects.webp` (800x1000)
* `/public/images/interests.webp` (800x1000)
* `/public/cv.pdf` (Your CV PDF)


5. **Run Development Server**:
```bash
npm run dev

